%I A114564 #12 Oct 06 2026 15:00:45
%S A114564 7,19,31,55,67,139,175,199,211,235,247,307,319,391,415,487,499,535,
%T A114564 571,595,631,679,715,787,811,931,1039,1075,1099,1135,1147,1255,1327,
%U A114564 1387,1399,1435,1459,1471,1507,1567,1639,1687,1759,1795,1819,1855
%N A114564 Numbers of the form 12s+7, where q=4s+3 is a prime for which the order of 2 is either q-1 or (q-1)/2.
%C A114564 Numbers of the form 3*q - 2 where q is a prime with primitive root -4 (A105876). - _Jianing Song_, Oct 06 2026
%D A114564 L. Heffter, Über das Problem der Nachbargebiete, Math. Ann., 38 (1891) 477-508.
%D A114564 G. Ringel, Map Color Theorem, Springer, 1974, p. 6.
%H A114564 Jianing Song, <a href="/A114564/b114564.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A114564 a(n) = 3*A105876(n) - 2.
%F A114564 a(n) = 6*A163778(n) + 1 = 12*A294434(n) + 7. - _Jianing Song_, Oct 05 2026
%o A114564 (PARI) isA114564(k) = if(k%12!=7, return(0)); my(p=(k+2)/3); return(isprime(p) && znorder(Mod(-4,p)) == p-1) \\ _Jianing Song_, Oct 06 2026
%Y A114564 Cf. A105876, A163778, A294434.
%K A114564 nonn,changed
%O A114564 1,1
%A A114564 _R. K. Guy_, Feb 11 2006
